    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d798">

                <pb facs="0949" n="855" sameAs="frus:frus1896/pg855"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Olney to
                            Mavroyeni Bey.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1896-04-15"><hi rendition="#italic">April 15,
                        1896</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 79.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have to acknowledge the receipt of your
                    note, special 17, of the 8th instant, communicating to me copy of an undated
                    telegram addressed to the first secretary of the Imperial Palace, to the Grand
                    Vizier, to the minister of foreign affairs, and to the Armenian patriarch, and
                    signed by a number of persons, apparently residents of Harpoot, protesting
                    against the presence and teachings of foreign missionaries in that city.</p>
                <p>It is believed that the vague charges enunciated in that telegram against foreign
                    missionaries are but one incident in a campaign of systematic misrepresentation
                    and calumny. If it be asserted by your Government that these charges lie at the
                    door of the American missionaries and teachers in Harpoot they may deserve
                    investigation, not because of their probability, but in order that such campaign
                    of prejudice and misstatement may be exposed.</p>
                <p>This Government will therefore set on foot inquiry to test the truth of the
                    charges and the genuineness of the memorial in question.</p>
                <p>Accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Richard Olney.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
